WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.489 --> 00:00:04.870
On February 13, The Batman director Matt Reeves
took to Twitter to share the first camera

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:09.420
test for the upcoming comic book adaptation
in which Robert Pattinson plays the Dark Knight.

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:14.620
It doesn't show very much of Pattinson's face,
but what the video lacks in direct face-time,

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:18.440
it makes up for in epic slow-motion pans of
Pattinson's Batman suit.

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:22.960
The clip is soaked in red light, and begins
with Pattinson walking toward the camera as

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:25.240
it focuses on the bat insignia on his costume.

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:29.140
As he turns to one side, we get a peek of
the shoulder pieces of the new suit and a

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:30.500
taste of the Battinson cape.

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:34.580
Then, finally, the lower half of Pattinson's
face comes into focus, with the upper half

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:36.200
shielded by his Batman mask.

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:40.880
Given the day it was dropped and its candy-red
color palette, this first video of Pattinson's

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:44.940
Batman could be considered something of a
Valentine's Day present from Reeves and the

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:46.200
folks at Warner Bros.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:46.700
Pictures.

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:50.440
From our vantage point, it looks as though
the film's team may have been inspired by

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:54.370
a few different versions of Batman's iconic
suit when they were working on the design

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:55.180
for the new movie.

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:59.420
The short video Matt Reeves released shows
a mechanical-looking Batman logo.

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:04.670
In the 2015 video game Batman: Arkham Knight,
the Batsuit armor pieces would mechanically

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:08.360
tighten, align, or separate depending on what
Batman wanted to do.

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:12.900
Arkham Origins also featured several different
shoulder armor options for the Batman suit

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:16.420
that look similar to what's shown in the camera
test clip Reeves shared online.

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:22.100
In Batman: Gotham Knight, the 2008 anthology
film comprised of animated superhero shorts,

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:25.399
Batman rocked a popped collar and a chin guard
in the "Crossfire" segment.

00:01:25.820 --> 00:01:31.820
Finally, in Gotham by Gaslight, an alternate-reality
Batman set in the 1880’s also wore a slightly

00:01:31.820 --> 00:01:34.140
popped collar while battling against Jack
the Ripper.

00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:38.180
There's even a theory going around that the
Batman insignia on this new suit is literally

00:01:38.189 --> 00:01:40.770
made from pieces of the gun that killed Bruce's
parents.

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:41.760
So, that's metal.

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:46.520
Regardless of how the costume came together
and what pieces of past Batman media it might

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:50.259
be referencing, the important thing is that
Pattinson loves how it looks.

00:01:50.260 --> 00:01:55.460
Speaking with Yahoo Entertainment in October
2019, Pattinson briefly gushed about his Batsuit:

00:01:55.820 --> 00:01:57.939
"Matt has got a really awesome idea about
it.

00:01:57.940 --> 00:02:00.280
I think this thing is going to be very, very
cool."

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:04.820
Luckily for everyone involved in The Batman,
reactions to the first camera test of Pattinson

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:07.360
in his Batsuit have been overwhelmingly positive.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:11.220
ComicBook.com's Brandon Davis wrote in response
to Reeves' tweet:

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:12.320
"IT'S BEAUTIFUL."

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:16.580
YouTuber and podcast host Eddy Burback was
so impressed with the video that he asked

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:18.460
for Reeves' hand in marriage, writing:

00:02:18.820 --> 00:02:19.900
"matt will you marry me"

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:24.820
After watching the camera test of Pattinson
as Batman, Awards Ace editor-in-chief Erick

00:02:24.820 --> 00:02:25.460
Weber tweeted:

00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:27.920
"CAN WE MAGICALLY MAKE IT 2021"

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:32.400
Finally, ReelBlend podcast co-host Kevin McCarthy
had a simple message for Reeves:

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:33.460
"Thank you, sir.

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:34.280
Hell yes."

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:39.080
Fans have reacted similarly, tweeting out
GIFs of people screaming with glee and straight-up

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:41.980
yelling to express just how happy they were
with the test footage.

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:43.060
One user tweeted:

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:44.360
"Thank you Matt Reeves.

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:47.020
I was like legit dying for Batman news.

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:47.560
Yes!!

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:48.540
Let's freaking go!!"

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:49.600
Another wrote:

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:51.800
"MATT REEVES .. I owe you my life.

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:52.810
This is magnificent.

00:02:52.810 --> 00:02:53.300
Thank you.

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:53.800
Thank you.

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:54.300
Thank you."

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:59.260
Yet another fan was particularly intrigued
by the finer details of the suit, what role

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:02.820
it might play in the upcoming film, and the
prospect of how the costume would hold up

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:04.640
over the course of The Batman and beyond:

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:06.140
"The textures.

00:03:06.159 --> 00:03:07.159
The stitches.

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:07.980
It's amateur, it's handmade.

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:09.960
It's just past the beginning of the Bat.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:11.020
It's so beautiful.

00:03:11.020 --> 00:03:14.420
I can't even imagine how the suit is going
to damage/evolve through the course of the

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:14.920
movies."

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:18.960
It's plain to see people are giddily picking
up what Reeves is putting down.

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:24.340
Even though The Batman is still incredibly
far out from its June 25, 2021 release date,

00:03:24.350 --> 00:03:28.430
this first look at Robert Pattinson's version
of the character promises even better things

00:03:28.430 --> 00:03:30.740
to come as the film gets closer to theaters.

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:34.080
We can't wait to see what the new version
of Gotham City looks like:

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:42.160
"This city... this city is a labyrinth, designed
to mock me!"

00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:47.100
Expectations are high and the standard is
now set — we officially can't wait to meet

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:47.880
The Batman.

